"disk:\n"
"it disappears when you shut down, and on a machine without much RAM a large\n"
"application can make the trial session unstable. Installing Dagric first "
"avoids\n"
"both, and the app is then permanent."
msgstr ""
"NOTA — questa è la prova live avviata dalla chiavetta USB.\n"
"Tutto ciò che installi ora resta nella memoria di questo computer, non su "
"un\n"
"disco: sparisce allo spegnimento e, su una macchina con poca RAM, un "
"programma\n"
"grande può rendere instabile la sessione di prova. Installando prima Dagric "
"si\n"
"evitano entrambe le cose e l'applicazione diventa definitiva."

#. TRANSLATORS: a space-separated list of the words that mean YES at a
#. "[y/N]" prompt in your language, lower case, shortest first. English
#. "y" and "yes" are always accepted as well — do not remove them, and do
#. not translate them. German: "j ja y yes". French: "o oui y yes".
#: config/includes.chroot/usr/bin/dagric-i18n.sh:231
msgid "y yes"
msgstr "s si sì y yes"

#. TRANSLATORS: every indented line under "To remove it completely" is a COMMAND
#. typed verbatim into a terminal — translate the prose around them, never the
#. commands themselves. "Ollama" is a product name.
#.
#. The old version of this screen said removal was `sudo rm -f
#. /usr/local/bin/ollama` and stopped there. That is wrong: Ollama's installer
#. also creates a systemd service, a system user, and a model directory, so
#. deleting the binary leaves an enabled service behind pointing at nothing. It
#. also never mentioned that a background service gets enabled at all — which on
#. an OS that sells itself on privacy is exactly the kind of thing the owner is
#. entitled to hear BEFORE saying yes, not discover later in systemctl.
#: config/includes.chroot/usr/bin/dagric-ai:22
msgid ""
"Dagric local AI setup\n"
"=======================\n"
"This installs Ollama, a local large-language-model runner:\n"
"  * models run entirely on this computer (GPU-accelerated when available)\n"
"  * works offline; nothing is sent anywhere\n"
"\n"
"What it changes on this machine:\n"
"  * installs the ollama binary and adds a system user for it\n"
"  * enables a background service that starts at boot and listens only on\n"
"    this computer (127.0.0.1 port 11434) — not reachable from your network\n"
"  * downloaded models land in /usr/share/ollama and can be several GB each\n"
"\n"
"To remove it completely:\n"
"  sudo systemctl disable --now ollama\n"
"  sudo rm -f /usr/local/bin/ollama /etc/systemd/system/ollama.service\n"
"  sudo rm -rf /usr/share/ollama\n"
"  sudo userdel ollama\n"
msgstr ""
"Configurazione IA locale di Dagric\n"
"=======================\n"
"Questo installa Ollama, un motore locale per grandi modelli linguistici:\n"
"  * i modelli girano interamente su questo computer (GPU usata se "
"disponibile)\n"
"  * funziona offline; non invia nulla a nessuno\n"
"\n"
"Cosa cambia su questa macchina:\n"
"  * installa il binario ollama e crea un utente di sistema dedicato\n"
"  * attiva un servizio in background che parte all'avvio e ascolta solo\n"
"    su questo computer (127.0.0.1 porta 11434) — irraggiungibile dalla tua "
"rete\n"
"  * i modelli scaricati finiscono in /usr/share/ollama, anche diversi GB "
"l'uno\n"
"\n"
"Per rimuoverlo completamente:\n"
"  sudo systemctl disable --now ollama\n"
"  sudo rm -f /usr/local/bin/ollama /etc/systemd/system/ollama.service\n"
"  sudo rm -rf /usr/share/ollama\n"
"  sudo userdel ollama\n"

#: config/includes.chroot/usr/bin/dagric-ai:41
msgid "Install Ollama from https://ollama.com? [y/N]"
msgstr "Installare Ollama da https://ollama.com? [s/N]"

